    "fidelity": "not-applicable",
    "note": "The finished design was read from Wichmann’s MOR0719 drawing. Its tile corners were snapped to the square-root-of-two grid in small-star-radius units. The unit-star opening is shared with the other Moroccan reconstructions. After it almost every line is drawn through a crossing of the star’s sides, carried on, with earlier lines, and turned round O; two compass transfers set the lines of the rosettes at the tile’s corners. The drawing gives no steps; we devised the construction.",
    "changes": "The compass steps, their order and the named points are ours. The tile edges follow the plain drawing. The tile holds two rosettes, one at O and a quarter at each corner. The colours follow Wichmann’s drawing in the Marinid zellige palette. Wade’s photograph MOR 0719 was not checked.",
    "reviewed": "2026-10-26"
  },
